===== 2  1D chain: random walk vs Deng-Goddard / Wen
$ python -m mobility_tool mobility --lam 0.2 --path 5.0,30,2 --json chain_1d.json

T = 298.15 K   λ = 0.2000 eV   n = 3
  Path              r/Å     J/meV    count       k/s^-1        P
  P1            5.000    30.000     2   4.8290e+12   0.5000
  Diffusion coefficient D = 4.0242e-03 cm^2/s   [random walk D = Σ k r²/2n]
  Mobility   μ = 0.1566 cm^2/(V·s)
  (comparison) Deng–Goddard D = Σ r²kP/2n: μ = 0.0783 cm^2/(V·s), lower by 2.0×

Results written to chain_1d.json

===== 3  anthracene: neighbour dimers and Gaussian inputs
$ python -m mobility_tool crystal "../benchmark/1 structure/anthracene.cif" --cutoff 4.0 -o anthracene_inputs --program gaussian --method B3LYP --basis 6-31G(d) --nproc 16 --mem 32GB
Cell contains 2 molecules, atoms [24, 24]
Neighbours 14, equivalent groups 5
